const judgments={
'cipher-study-routing':[false,'Preset assistant chooses an MCQ repair chapter, offers a sprint and optionally supplies a Pro flashcard deck.','HOLD: learner text describes best next move, missed concepts and a prepared 10-question sprint, but context uses latest MCQ IDs plus historical chapter accuracy, not canonical concept diagnosis. The same question corrected later can still drive lowest historical accuracy, and orphan IDs can supply a chapter fallback. Supplied assistant content precedes weak/starter rebuilding without checking alignment. Preset disclosure is present and useful, but it does not validate those stronger targeting/preparation claims. No FAQ, pricing/payment outcome or external service promise is approved.'],
'daily-challenges':[false,'Local weekday chooses one fixed five-MCQ set used by the full challenge and landing widget.','HOLD: all seven current weekday lists resolve to five local MCQs, and the schedule repeats rather than adapting to a learner. The two consumers recompute a new date-keyed question list but retain question index, selection and results across an enduring mount. A calendar rollover can therefore change the question under existing progress without a challenge-identity reset. This is a source-derived conditional transition, not an observed live failure; a whole daily-session/routing claim needs a defined rollover boundary. Unrendered descriptions are not treated as surfaced promises. No streak, reward or coin operation was executed.'],
'deep-dive-recommendations':[false,'Legacy lesson ranking combines objective/topic/domain hints and lexical overlap over missed-question fields.','HOLD: the surfaced chosen-from-missed-concepts and match-description language is stronger than the grounding. Options and explanations change ranking and matched terms even for an otherwise unrelated synthetic prompt; those can be distractors or supplied solution text rather than demonstrated misunderstandings. Unknown domains can yield no result, and domain fallback follows the first miss. Existing lesson IDs and deterministic scores establish routing behavior, not approved concept/teaching links or recovered weakness. Destinations keep their own independent holds.'],
'diagnostic':[false,'Five short easy questions, one per chapter where a native candidate or authored fallback exists, seed later MCQ review.','HOLD: the current default includes m032 with an RTO glossary link in the stem before submission, while the interface calls this a mini mock test/baseline. A single sampled answer per domain and assisted recall do not establish missed canonical concepts. The summary announces personalized Smart Review before the completion callback saves; failure handling can still mark the baseline done. Empty native pools fall back to separately held starter identities, without proving those assessment/feedback contracts. Native/starter question and feedback judgments are not requalified by this selector review.'],
'exam-selection':[false,'Timed local practice samples non-enrichment PBQs first and MCQs second, with saved-session resume and result review.','HOLD: selection can underfill a requested size and voucher consumption precedes pool construction. Saved questions are reused without current-revision resampling, and a saved zero timer falls through to the configured duration. The composition UI permits all-PBQ runs; inline glossary support also remains available before answers. The explicit practice-not-official-scoring disclaimer is preserved and is not called an official-score claim. These selection/resume/assistance limits prevent qualification as a coherent timed-assessment selector; no voucher, storage, timer or result write occurred.'],
'flashcard-navigation':[false,'Catalogue, chapter, current-ID shared/saved decks and assistant requests resolve a deck/mode for study.','HOLD: matching saved IDs take precedence over native catalogue IDs, so a native URL is not exclusive or revision-pinned content. Shared parsing drops unknown IDs but keeps duplicates; two occurrences of one ID can flow to the pass whose completion counts distinct IDs. Native current decks remain useful, but the generalized input/identity contract is ambiguous and can make completion unreachable. Persisting new generated sets with a prefix does not retroactively normalize all hydrated inputs. No actual saved account state, collision or corrupted deck was fetched or written.'],
'flashcard-study-pass':[false,'Flip, move, shuffle, self-rate, complete a pass and continue to another deck or lesson.','HOLD: pass completion counts distinct rated identities irrespective of Again/Got it; mastered is a self-rated label rather than measured retention. More concretely, duplicated incoming card IDs can make the distinct-ID completion threshold unreachable. All-Again completion does not itself increase the mastered count; those two signals are kept distinct. Native-container content qualifications do not approve this broader state/presentation contract or turn a reveal/selection into independent mastery evidence.'],
'glossary-delivery':[true,'Case-insensitive inline term matching exposes the bound glossary entry on pointer or keyboard activation.','Qualified only as an explicit definition-reveal mechanism. Longest-first matching uses non-alphanumeric boundaries within formatting segments; formatting can break a longer phrase. Outside pointer interaction closes the popup, and Enter/Space toggle it. Plain React text rendering does not interpret input markup. No word-sense disambiguation, dictionary correctness, human approval or canonical mapping is inferred. It is assistance wherever a consumer renders it, including assessment options/stems; this qualification does not approve an unassisted exam/diagnostic claim or clear any held glossary entry.'],
'lesson-navigation':[false,'Profile-ordered/searchable gated lessons deliver keywords, authored sections/traps, reveal-only checks and three derived practice items.','HOLD: the learner end action promises related flashcards/matching acronyms, but selection takes the first deck with any overlapping broad objective and otherwise the first catalogue deck. The resilience/recovery lesson can select the security-principles/access deck with no RTO/RPO/MTD/MTTR card. Search, optional flags and existing Pro/free-preview gates are source-proven; self-marked completion and best recall percentage do not supply mastery or validate this remediation link. All source-container/content holds remain independent.'],
'lesson-related-pbq':[false,'Lesson actions launch a ten-question chapter review or choose a same-chapter/access fallback PBQ.','HOLD: the related label is not grounded in a specific skill. With no requested-chapter candidate, an accessible preview from another chapter can be selected; when the first same-chapter candidate is locked, it can block that accessible fallback and route to access UI. Chapter/type/entitlement routing is useful legacy behavior but not an approved teaching link. No unlock, wallet interaction, learner navigation or current private-bank query occurred.'],
'next-flashcard-deck':[true,'Continue-studying chooses the cyclic successor in the authored deck catalogue.','Qualified strictly as ordered navigation: all 29 current native decks advance to the next source entry, the last wraps to the first, unknown/null current IDs choose the first and an empty injected catalogue yields null. There is no learner-history or concept criterion. A destination keeps its own content/hold status; no relevance, novelty, improved retention, family independence or mastery is approved.'],
'next-related-pbq':[false,'Next-question helper prefers never-correct same chapter/type, then same chapter, then a cyclic successor.','HOLD: the surfaced Try a different PBQ label is not guaranteed for a valid one-item runtime bank, which returns the current question. An unknown current ID falls to the first source row, and any historical correct attempt excludes a candidate from preferred branches even if later missed. Empty runtime input falls back to the local bank. These exact branches establish coarse navigation, not reliable difference, concept relatedness or independently novel evidence. The signed-in caller restricts this action to Pro; no production entitlement state was observed.'],
'pbq-catalogue-selection':[false,'Browse/filter/paginate/star PBQs and use Pro random practice with unseen/historically-missed priorities.','HOLD: empty bank or load error returns upgrade UI independently of the actual tier, so even a Pro empty/error state is represented as an access upgrade rather than a distinct data failure. History also permits the same ID in ever-correct and ever-missed sets; the list ranks ever-correct rows last rather than using latest correctness. Random practice uses the whole bank rather than the visible filtered list and falls back to the last source row when exhausted. Those limits must remain explicit before approving the whole workspace/recommended-review claim. No payment, unlock, live load failure or account history was exercised.']
};
